From: beitlab Robotics MilkV duo OS <image/patches>
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] duos arm64 sd: include the playground device tree fragment

Local change. The fragment itself lives in duo-s-playground at
image/dts/playground_duos.dtsi and is copied next to the board dts by
scripts/build-image.sh, so the DT source of truth stays in the playground
repository. The SDK kernel-dts rule symlinks every *.dts* of dts_arm64/
into arch/arm64/boot/dts/cvitek/, so the include resolves there.

The fragment adds the C906L carveout and remoteproc node from 7221d232
(Milk-V v1 `arduino` branch) and disables the Linux claims on the carrier
pads; it is quoted in docs/sdk-notes.md.
---
diff --git a/build/boards/cv181x/sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd.dts b/build/boards/cv181x/sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd.dts
index 6e243a58..52e9a60d 100644
--- a/build/boards/cv181x/sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd.dts
+++ b/build/boards/cv181x/sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd/dts_arm64/sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd.dts
@@ -111,3 +111,8 @@
 &uart4 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/* beitlab Robotics MilkV duo OS: C906L remoteproc and carrier pad release.
+ * The file is installed next to this one by scripts/build-image.sh from
+ * duo-s-playground/image/dts/playground_duos.dtsi. */
+#include "playground_duos.dtsi"
